From 7e50aab46ca5bdfa10f6d1d77d75b93a55b2bde1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 18:03:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08376/11362] exp6091: analyse full 24-cell shard; ack inert
 arc_competition_agent.py drift

Primary exact-match still flat (0 discordant, p=1.0, unchanged from
the 18-cell checkpoint) -- underpowered at n=11 games, not a
refutation. Mechanism contrast (treatment vs control fidelity)
firmed up: p=0.0078 -> p=0.0039.

11 stale-flagged artifacts drift on the same single-line change
(84d4b2fe2b added one noqa:F401-marked unused import to
arc_competition_agent.py, nothing else) -- acknowledged as
verified-inert per artifact_freshness_lint's hash-pinned schema.

One downstream cascade (outer_loop_arc_gateway_accurate_rescore)
got a THIRD acknowledgement appended rather than a rebuild: a
rebuild attempt reproduced every number byte-identically but
silently dropped all 10 prior freshness_acknowledgements entries
plus a 2026-07-30 corrigendum block -- a real never-prune defect
in the rebuild tooling, not something to paper over by committing
its output.
