     "reason": "REQ-ARC-WMTE-6090, DEFAULT OFF. The change is two imports plus a single branch in E3AgentPolicy: `_induce_rows = active_transitions`, replaced by the held-out-stripped list ONLY when `cegis_accept_split_enabled()` reads CARNOT_ARC_CEGIS_ACCEPT_SPLIT as truthy. That variable is unset in every path that produced this artifact, so the induce() call receives the identical object it received before. No threshold, no ordering, no seed, no control flow moves.",
     "evidence": "TWO INDEPENDENT LINES. (1) TEST: tests/python/test_arc_cegis_accept_split_gate_20260803.py and tests/python/test_arc_refactor_write_collapse_instrumentation_20260803.py run the affected paths in BOTH flag directions and assert that flag-OFF reproduces the shipped behaviour exactly, including a trajectory-invariance assertion for the OFF direction; every added pattern was mutation-proved by deletion (suite goes red). (2) EMPIRICAL REBUILD, which is stronger than argument: results/arc_gateway_card_ground_truth_20260727.json was FULLY REBUILT against this exact working tree on 2026-08-03 (374.2s, 48/48 cells, all 6 games x 3 seeds replayed through E3AgentPolicy with the LLM off). Every scientific figure came back byte-identical: the verdict string still reads real_median_optimism 0.018097 vs modelled 0.036903, model wrong on 17 of 44 cells, 6 sign-flipped, and every per-cell off/res/card/real/m2/repro value was unchanged. The ONLY deltas were 48 wall-clock timings (machine load, the conductor was running), the provenance hashes, and the content checksum. That rebuild was then REVERTED, deliberately: it silently dropped all 5 pre-existing freshness_acknowledgement blocks on that artifact, which is a never-prune violation executed by the rebuild tooling.",
     "why_not_rebuilt": "A rebuild_command IS registered, and the lint's docstring rightly prefers rebuilding. It was tried, on the cheapest artifact of the twelve, and the result is recorded above: it changed no scientific figure and DESTROYED 5 hand-written acknowledgement blocks. Repeating that across the remaining artifacts would rewrite hundreds of published wall-clock measurements and destroy roughly a hundred never-prune records to prove something the rebuild already proved once. The rebuild tooling dropping freshness_acknowledgements is a defect worth fixing before it is used as the routine path; until then this acknowledgement is the non-destructive option, and it follows the precedent set by the 5 prior default-OFF changes to this same file, each of which was cleared this way rather than by rebuild."
+   },
+   {
+    "path": "python/carnot/agentic/arc_competition_agent.py",
+    "sha256_was": "09af1f68207c6293e8f6978a5cd0ae7c105d3829ece79d90f88a88f8b2c69177",
+    "sha256_now": "10536d30c22478d9beee770ad7a0a9fa1877777b22f8c2e72dd8765d23d03dda",
+    "reason": "2026-08-06 conductor commit 84d4b2fe2b added exactly one line to this file: an unused import (`import carnot.agentic.arc_task_aware_energy as arc_task_aware_energy  # noqa: F401`). No existing statement, function body, or control path was touched.",
+    "evidence": "`diff` between the pre- and post-commit blobs (git show 84d4b2fe2b~1 vs 84d4b2fe2b) is a single added import line, self-declared unused via noqa: F401. An import-only addition cannot change the behavior of any code path that does not reference the new module, and nothing in this artifact's generating script references arc_task_aware_energy."
    }
   ]
